+# Book text is arbitrary prose, not a prompt: a book *about* language models quotes
+# "<|endoftext|>" and friends as literal strings. tiktoken refuses to encode those by
+# default and raises ValueError, which kills the whole translation process mid-run with
+# no way to resume past it. disallowed_special=() makes tiktoken treat every special
+# marker as ordinary text, which is exactly what it is here - we only ever use these
+# token counts to size request groups, never to feed tokens to a model.
+_NO_SPECIAL: tuple[str, ...] = ()
+
 
